+   runs out WRAPS — left-ruled, so each line starts at the first line's x — and the seam is the
+   same 0.45rem in both axes.
+   `contain: inline-size`: the line adds nothing to the rail's max-content, so the card's width is
+   the crib's (fine) or the strip's (coarse) exactly as before and the board cannot walk.
+   Coarse: a chip GROWS to fill its line, so a line holding one chip is the column's 168 × 44
+   chip, byte-identical, and a thumb's box never shrinks (M01); `md:text-left` keeps the word and
+   its scribble at the left of a grown chip. */
+.options-line {
+  display: flex;
+  flex-wrap: wrap;
+  justify-content: flex-start;
+  contain: inline-size;
+}
+
+.options-line > .ctrl-btn {
+  flex: 0 0 auto;
+}
+
+@media (pointer: coarse) {
+  .options-line > .ctrl-btn {
+    flex: 1 1 auto;
+  }
+}
+
 .options-pair > .ctrl-btn {
   flex: 1 1 0;
 }
